1
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:03,569
You blink about fifteen times a minute.

2
00:00:04,469 --> 00:00:06,876
Each blink lasts about
a tenth of a second.

3
00:00:07,776 --> 00:00:09,262
You don't even notice them.

4
00:00:10,362 --> 00:00:11,162
It does.

5
00:00:14,428 --> 00:00:15,820
This is SCP-173.

6
00:00:15,820 --> 00:00:17,734
It's made of concrete.

7
00:00:17,734 --> 00:00:21,736
And it cannot move while
you're looking at it.

8
00:00:22,236 --> 00:00:25,527
It was the very first SCP ever written.

9
00:00:25,527 --> 00:00:28,902
The reason the entire Foundation exists.

10
00:00:29,352 --> 00:00:32,000
And in 2022, it officially lost its face.

11
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:37,183
This is the complete story of SCP-173.

12
00:00:37,183 --> 00:00:38,697
Try not to blink.

13
00:00:44,397 --> 00:00:47,082
Every SCP file starts the same way.

14
00:00:47,082 --> 00:00:48,770
This one did it first.

15
00:00:49,270 --> 00:00:51,597
Item number: SCP-173.

16
00:00:51,597 --> 00:00:53,924
Object class: Euclid.

17
00:00:54,374 --> 00:00:56,416
Euclid means it can be contained...

18
00:00:56,416 --> 00:00:59,684
but it's unpredictable, and
nobody fully understands it.

19
00:01:00,284 --> 00:01:04,604
According to the file, it
was moved to Site-19 in 1993.

20
00:01:04,604 --> 00:01:07,746
Where it came from is listed as unknown.

21
00:01:08,346 --> 00:01:12,186
It's made of concrete and rebar,
with traces of spray paint.

22
00:01:12,186 --> 00:01:15,002
A brand you could buy
at any hardware store.

23
00:01:15,502 --> 00:01:17,523
Which means that, at some point...

24
00:01:17,523 --> 00:01:18,653
someone painted it.

25
00:01:19,553 --> 00:01:21,698
And it's not just a statue.

26
00:01:21,698 --> 00:01:23,764
The file calls it animate.

27
00:01:23,764 --> 00:01:25,513
And extremely hostile.

28
00:01:29,413 --> 00:01:33,401
Everything about SCP-173
comes down to one rule.

29
00:01:33,851 --> 00:01:36,751
It cannot move while it's
in a direct line of sight.

30
00:01:37,151 --> 00:01:39,760
And that line of sight must not be broken.

31
00:01:39,760 --> 00:01:40,560
At any time.

32
00:01:41,205 --> 00:01:42,847
Nobody has ever seen it move.

33
00:01:42,847 --> 00:01:44,432
Because if you can see it...

34
00:01:44,432 --> 00:01:45,232
it can't.

35
00:01:45,942 --> 00:01:48,597
But the moment nobody's looking, it can.

36
00:01:48,597 --> 00:01:51,717
And the file lists exactly
two ways it attacks.

37
00:01:52,167 --> 00:01:55,021
It snaps the neck, at
the base of the skull.

38
00:01:55,021 --> 00:01:56,059
Or it strangles.

39
00:01:56,859 --> 00:02:02,698
After an attack, staff follow something
called Class 4 hazardous object containment

40
00:02:02,698 --> 00:02:03,498
procedures.

41
00:02:03,472 --> 00:02:05,935
The file never says what those are.

42
00:02:06,705 --> 00:02:08,186
So the rule sounds simple.

43
00:02:08,186 --> 00:02:09,554
Just keep looking at it.

44
00:02:10,054 --> 00:02:11,296
The problem is...

45
00:02:11,296 --> 00:02:12,096
you can't.

46
00:02:16,327 --> 00:02:20,084
Every few seconds, for about a
tenth of a second, you're blind.

47
00:02:20,084 --> 00:02:21,158
You can't stop it.

48
00:02:21,158 --> 00:02:21,958
Nobody can.

49
00:02:22,364 --> 00:02:24,113
So nobody goes in alone.

50
00:02:24,513 --> 00:02:28,389
The file says no fewer than three
people may enter its container.

51
00:02:28,389 --> 00:02:30,476
And the door is locked behind them.

52
00:02:30,876 --> 00:02:36,094
Two of them must keep direct eye
contact with SCP-173 the entire time...

53
00:02:36,094 --> 00:02:39,863
until everyone is out, and
the door is locked again.

54
00:02:40,313 --> 00:02:41,113
Two watchers.

55
00:02:41,057 --> 00:02:44,435
So when one of them blinks,
the other one is still looking.

56
00:02:44,885 --> 00:02:45,685
Sounds safe.

57
00:02:45,671 --> 00:02:47,112
But let's do the math.

58
00:02:47,712 --> 00:02:52,871
If two people blink at a normal rate, at
random, sooner or later they blink at the

59
00:02:52,871 --> 00:02:54,003
exact same moment.

60
00:02:54,466 --> 00:02:57,501
On average, that would happen
roughly once every minute.

61
00:02:57,951 --> 00:03:01,175
Both of them blind, for a
few hundredths of a second.

62
00:03:01,675 --> 00:03:05,401
The file never says how fast SCP-173 is.

63
00:03:05,401 --> 00:03:07,171
It doesn't need to.

64
00:03:07,971 --> 00:03:12,625
That's why there's one more line in the
procedures: personnel must alert one another

65
00:03:12,625 --> 00:03:13,511
before blinking.

66
00:03:14,467 --> 00:03:15,347
[radio] Blinking.

67
00:03:15,417 --> 00:03:16,317
[radio] Watching.

68
00:03:16,467 --> 00:03:17,267
[radio] Clear.

69
00:03:18,067 --> 00:03:19,009
[radio] Blinking.

70
00:03:19,017 --> 00:03:19,955
[radio] Watching.

71
00:03:20,567 --> 00:03:22,486
Every blink, called out loud.

72
00:03:22,486 --> 00:03:24,803
For as long as you're in that room.

73
00:03:25,303 --> 00:03:26,355
And the third person?

74
00:03:26,355 --> 00:03:28,458
The third person isn't watching it at all.

75
00:03:32,358 --> 00:03:35,357
Because there's something
on the floor of the cell.

76
00:03:35,357 --> 00:03:36,886
A reddish-brown substance.

77
00:03:37,336 --> 00:03:38,755
The file is specific.

78
00:03:38,755 --> 00:03:40,781
It's a combination of feces...

79
00:03:40,781 --> 00:03:41,581
and blood.

80
00:03:41,956 --> 00:03:44,096
And the origin of both is unknown.

81
00:03:44,696 --> 00:03:47,873
The enclosure has to be
cleaned on a bi-weekly basis.

82
00:03:48,323 --> 00:03:50,838
So, on a schedule, three people walk in.

83
00:03:50,838 --> 00:03:53,792
Two of them stare at a
statue without stopping.

84
00:03:53,792 --> 00:03:56,747
And one of them mops the
floor around its feet.

85
00:03:57,447 --> 00:03:58,517
Whose blood is it?

86
00:03:58,517 --> 00:03:59,707
The file never says.

87
00:04:03,807 --> 00:04:06,830
And then there's the line most
people find the creepiest.

88
00:04:07,280 --> 00:04:11,789
Staff report the sound of scraping stone
coming from inside the container...

89
00:04:11,789 --> 00:04:13,213
when no one is in there.

90
00:04:13,813 --> 00:04:15,446
The file calls this normal.

91
00:04:16,346 --> 00:04:17,432
Think about it.

92
00:04:17,432 --> 00:04:20,545
When the room is empty,
nobody is watching.

93
00:04:20,545 --> 00:04:21,414
So it moves.

94
00:04:21,414 --> 00:04:25,469
Concrete dragging across
concrete, behind a locked door.

95
00:04:26,169 --> 00:04:30,546
Any change in this behaviour is to be
reported to the supervisor on duty.

96
00:04:30,996 --> 00:04:33,885
The file doesn't say what
a change would sound like.

97
00:04:33,885 --> 00:04:34,685
Louder?

98
00:04:34,273 --> 00:04:35,329
Closer to the door?

99
00:04:36,029 --> 00:04:36,879
Or one night...

100
00:04:37,879 --> 00:04:38,679
silence.

101
00:04:40,636 --> 00:04:43,400
And here's something
the file never answers.

102
00:04:43,400 --> 00:04:45,347
Does a camera count as looking?

103
00:04:45,347 --> 00:04:47,798
Tell me what you think in the comments.

104
00:04:51,698 --> 00:04:54,218
Now here's the part
most people don't know.

105
00:04:54,718 --> 00:04:56,007
June 22nd, 2007.

106
00:04:56,007 --> 00:05:00,358
Someone posts anonymously on
4chan's paranormal board.

107
00:05:00,808 --> 00:05:02,540
A photo of a strange statue.

108
00:05:02,540 --> 00:05:07,055
And under it, a few paragraphs written
like a classified government file.

109
00:05:07,455 --> 00:05:08,291
Item number.

110
00:05:08,291 --> 00:05:09,197
Object class.

111
00:05:09,197 --> 00:05:11,358
Special containment procedures.

112
00:05:11,958 --> 00:05:12,824
People loved it.

113
00:05:12,824 --> 00:05:14,720
And they started writing their own.

114
00:05:15,170 --> 00:05:17,158
By January 2008, there was a wiki.

115
00:05:17,158 --> 00:05:20,725
That summer, it moved to the
site where it still lives today.

116
00:05:21,175 --> 00:05:25,213
Today there are over
ten thousand SCP files.

117
00:05:25,213 --> 00:05:26,013
096.

118
00:05:25,580 --> 00:05:26,380
682.

119
00:05:25,947 --> 00:05:31,911
Nearly all of them still follow
the format this one post started.

120
00:05:32,361 --> 00:05:34,720
Its author was later identified.

121
00:05:34,720 --> 00:05:36,047
He goes by Moto42.

122
00:05:36,747 --> 00:05:39,251
There's even a strange coincidence.

123
00:05:39,251 --> 00:05:44,975
Less than two weeks before that post, a
TV episode aired about statues that only

124
00:05:44,975 --> 00:05:46,907
move when nobody's looking.

125
00:05:46,907 --> 00:05:50,413
People still debate whether
that was an accident.

126
00:05:51,085 --> 00:05:56,666
And in 2012, a free game called SCP:
Containment Breach turned the rule into a

127
00:05:56,666 --> 00:05:57,466
mechanic.

128
00:05:57,310 --> 00:05:58,885
A meter that drains...

129
00:05:58,885 --> 00:06:00,960
until you're forced to blink.

130
00:06:01,482 --> 00:06:06,076
For a lot of people, that was the
first time they ever met SCP-173.

131
00:06:09,976 --> 00:06:11,461
But there's one more twist.

132
00:06:11,461 --> 00:06:14,594
The statue in that photo was
never meant to be a monster.

133
00:06:15,044 --> 00:06:16,865
It was a real sculpture.

134
00:06:17,215 --> 00:06:21,467
Untitled 2004, by the
Japanese artist Izumi Kato.

135
00:06:21,867 --> 00:06:23,951
And it was used without his permission.

136
00:06:24,451 --> 00:06:26,987
In 2014, the wiki reached out to him.

137
00:06:26,987 --> 00:06:30,756
He reluctantly allowed it,
for non-commercial use only.

138
00:06:31,206 --> 00:06:34,435
But people kept selling merchandise
with his sculpture on it anyway.

139
00:06:34,935 --> 00:06:39,216
So in February 2022, the
SCP wiki removed the photo.

140
00:06:39,216 --> 00:06:42,591
And Moto42 asked that nothing replace it.

141
00:06:43,191 --> 00:06:44,994
Which means today...

142
00:06:44,994 --> 00:06:47,789
SCP-173 officially has no face.

143
00:06:48,689 --> 00:06:52,461
Every version you've ever seen
is somebody's own design.

144
00:06:52,461 --> 00:06:53,472
Including ours.

145
00:06:53,472 --> 00:06:56,571
Ours is built from exactly
what the file says.

146
00:06:56,571 --> 00:06:57,371
Concrete.

147
00:06:57,177 --> 00:06:57,977
Rebar.

148
00:06:57,582 --> 00:06:58,390
Spray paint.

149
00:06:58,390 --> 00:06:59,266
Nothing more.

150
00:06:59,866 --> 00:07:05,196
The real SCP-173 is whatever you
see when you close your eyes.

151
00:07:06,796 --> 00:07:09,965
The entire file is barely
more than two hundred words.

152
00:07:09,965 --> 00:07:13,075
And it's been scaring people
for almost twenty years.

153
00:07:13,575 --> 00:07:16,183
Because it was never
really about a statue.

154
00:07:16,183 --> 00:07:19,761
It's about the one thing your
body does without asking you.

155
00:07:20,461 --> 00:07:23,337
You've blinked dozens of times
since this video started.

156
00:07:23,937 --> 00:07:26,159
Every single one was a chance.

157
00:07:29,059 --> 00:07:29,862
Don't blink.

158
00:07:32,362 --> 00:07:36,862
SCP-173 is the one you
can never stop looking at.

159
00:07:36,862 --> 00:07:40,628
SCP-096 is the one you can never look at.

160
00:07:40,628 --> 00:07:43,659
Its complete story is right here.

